{"step_index":274,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:56:56Z","thinking":"The user has requested document creation across multiple collections. Consideration is needed regarding which collection to prioritize. The available tool appears suitable for either prompting the user for a preferred choice or offering a recommendation.\n\n\nConsidering the user's implicit intent, initiating a multiple-choice question to determine the desired publication collection seems appropriate. This action directly addresses the ambiguity of the user's request, ensuring the document is properly organized. The default publish setting will likely be correct.\n\n\nA phased migration is the chosen strategy, domain by domain, starting with the smallest. Dovecot will authenticate directly against the existing LDAP servers during the transition. This approach maintains a single source of truth for email accounts, facilitating rollback.\n\n\nAnalysis reveals a probable primary LDAP source, confirmed to be independent of the target data. Observed data anomalies include malformed email addresses with double \"@\" symbols, indicating source data corruption. A legacy email format and inconsistent account status require systemic resolution before integration.\n\n\nPassword hashing uses SHA-1, a Dovecot-supported scheme; no immediate password resets are needed. Two Maildir path conventions exist, requiring migration tools to handle both formats. The `smtp-mtq-1` server decommissioning necessitates LDAP relocation to a persistent host.\n\nDomain `ool.fr` was chosen as the pilot, a smaller domain with clean data and active mailboxes. The migration plan is progressing. Phase 1 authentication architecture is validated. Phase 2 LDAP attribute mapping is complete.\n\n\nLDAP configuration within Dovecot 2.4 presents a challenge; the older method is deprecated. The new embedded syntax remains elusive despite testing various parameter names, and official documentation is unavailable. The system may require an additional package to enable LDAP support for passdb/userdb, a hypothesis requiring verification. Currently, LDAP authentication fails with the built-in configuration, suggesting missing dependencies.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_question","args":{"questions":"[{\"is_multi_select\":false,\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Infra (bda1a3da-cc3d-4c5d-92d1-d831dfbe2eae)\",\"Projets (03d7f507-0722-46bb-ab83-474b42ba6a1c)\",\"Test_RAG (a18d1aba-f621-430f-9a37-4a723d38e16c)\"],\"question\":\"In which Outline collection would you like me to create and publish this document?\"}]","toolAction":"\"Asking collection preference\"","toolSummary":"\"Ask user for target collection\""}}]}
