{"step_index":276,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:57:22Z","thinking":"Determining the necessary parameters for the document upload to the target system's create endpoint. The `collectionId`, `title`, and `text` data, along with a `publish` flag, will be constructed into the request body. Preparing the Python script or equivalent command now.\n\n\nConsidering a potential certificate issue with the preferred method, the approach shifted to utilizing a command-line tool known for its robustness in handling such situations, creating a temporary file for the JSON payload. This will allow for the sending of a POST request, verifying the response, and cleaning up the temporary file afterward. The next step is crafting the request body with carefully formatted French Markdown content.\n\n\nThe plan is to migrate the email service to a unified Postfix + Dovecot + Roundcube platform (`mtq-mailsrvp-01`), decommissioning legacy qmail servers gradually, domain by domain. Initial focus will be on the smallest and cleanest domain for pilot testing. Directory services will be handled by direct authentication against the existing LDAP source during the transition.\n\nDovecot will authenticate directly against the LDAP source using a dedicated read-only service account. This avoids directory migration and ensures both qmail and Postfix read from the same source. Data mapping reveals potential inconsistencies in the Guadeloupe/Guyana setups, likely due to application-level data duplication rather than native LDAP replication, and suggests that `172.30.37.225` might be the authoritative LDAP source.\n\n\nInitial investigation revealed an existing Postfix deployment on the target platform; a separate flat-file authentication mechanism is currently used.  A critical methodological note indicates LDAP searches are limited to 500 results, which led to inaccurate estimations; direct database reading is required for accurate counts. Data anomalies include corrupted email attributes, a legacy email format needing conversion, non-uniform account status, and SHA-1 password hashing. Two Maildir path conventions also coexist.\n\n\nThe migration tooling must handle both legacy configurations. The LDAP service currently running on the `smtp-mtq-1` server, which will be decommissioned, needs relocation to a persistent host as a separate task before the server is shut down.\n\nDomain `ool.fr` was selected as the pilot, it has clean data with real mailboxes. The other candidates, `rife.re` (forward-only accounts) and `business.ool.fr` (corrupted data), were excluded.\n\nThe authentication architecture, attribute mapping, and dedicated service account are complete. The filter logic for authentication, including whitelisting statuses and excluding forwards, has been validated. Connecting the LDAP passdb/userdb in Dovecot's authentication configuration is in progress.\n\n\nCurrently blocked on Dovecot LDAP configuration. The current Dovecot version's integrated LDAP configuration syntax differs from older methods. Several parameter variations have been tested unsuccessfully. The official documentation is unavailable, and third-party sources are inconsistent across versions.\n\nThe LDAP support for passdb/userdb might require an uninstalled, separate package. Checking for missing authentication modules and packages is necessary to confirm. There are other risks: Legacy webmail data conversion scope, a blocked queue on another server, account deduplication, and the location of contact data still need resolution. Also the traffic role for two servers is unclear.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c '\\nimport json, subprocess\\n\\ntitle = \\\"Migration qmail → Postfix/Dovecot — Outremer Telecom\\\"\\ncollection_id = \\\"bda1a3da-cc3d-4c5d-92d1-d831dfbe2eae\\\"\\n\\ndoc_text = \\\"\\\"\\\"**Statut** : En cours (phase du domaine pilote)  \\n**Dernière mise à jour** : 2026-09-22  \\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Vue d'\\\\''ensemble du projet\\n\\nOutremer Telecom exploite le service de messagerie sur trois sites régionaux — Martinique (mtq), Guadeloupe (gua) et Guyane (guy) — chacun avec sa propre infrastructure legacy qmail-ldap et son annuaire LDAP local. L'\\\\''objectif est de migrer l'\\\\''ensemble du service de messagerie vers une plateforme unifiée Postfix + Dovecot + Roundcube (`mtq-mailsrvp-01`), avec un décommissionnement progressif des serveurs qmail legacy.\\n\\n* **Stratégie** : Migration domaine par domaine plutôt qu'\\\\''une bascule unique, en commençant par le domaine le plus petit et le plus propre comme pilote avant d'\\\\''attaquer les domaines plus gros et plus risqués.\\n* **Décision d'\\\\''architecture** : Pendant la transition, les annuaires LDAP existants ne sont ni migrés ni copiés. Dovecot s'\\\\''authentifie directement contre le LDAP source, via le réseau, avec un compte de service dédié en lecture seule. Cela garantit que qmail et Postfix lisent tous les deux la même source de vérité, sans jamais diverger, et permet un retour arrière simple en cas de problème.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Cartographie de l'\\\\''infrastructure\\n\\n| Serveur | Rôle | Nombre réel de comptes | Remarques |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `smtp-mtq-1` | Source qmail-ldap Martinique | 64 492 | Sera définitivement éteint une fois qmail décommissionné |\\n| `smtp-guy-1` | Source qmail-ldap Guyane | 121 461 | Données quasi identiques à gua |\\n| `smtp-gua-1` | Source qmail-ldap Guadeloupe | 121 455 | Données quasi identiques à guy ; aucune réplication LDAP native trouvée (pas de syncrepl/contextCSN) — probablement une double écriture applicative |\\n| `172.30.37.225` | Serveur LDAP dont la signature correspond à guy/gua\n<truncated 7417 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Uploading document to Outline\"","toolSummary":"\"Create and publish doc in Outline\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
