{"step_index":282,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:58:24Z","content":"The document has been created and published in the **Infra** collection on Outline.\n\n---\n\n### Document Details\n\n* **Title**: `Migration qmail → Postfix/Dovecot — Outremer Telecom`\n* **Collection**: **Infra** (`bda1a3da-cc3d-4c5d-92d1-d831dfbe2eae`)\n* **Document ID**: `93ddf5d6-6091-4fd2-bf9d-063ada0212a3`\n* **Status**: **Published**\n* **Direct URL**: [https://wiki.corp.intranet.local/doc/migration-qmail-postfixdovecot-outremer-telecom-3eiPEr1MHO](https://wiki.corp.intranet.local/doc/migration-qmail-postfixdovecot-outremer-telecom-3eiPEr1MHO)\n\n---\n\n### Highlights Included in the Page\n\n1. **Architecture & Scope**: Regional setup across MTQ, GUA, and GUY; migration onto `mtq-mailsrvp-01`; direct read-only LDAP authentication approach.\n2. **Infrastructure Cartography**: Clean table of all 5 participating servers (`smtp-mtq-1`, `smtp-guy-1`, `smtp-gua-1`, `172.30.37.225`, and `mtq-mailsrvp-01`) with real account counts.\n3. **Data Quality Findings**: Documented issues regarding `mail` attribute corruption, 2012–2014 Sent-folder formats (`sentmail-*`), `accountStatus` values, `{SHA}` password scheme, and Maildir path conventions (`d1` vs `d2`).\n4. **Pilot Domain**: Rationale for selecting `ool.fr` (12 clean accounts) over `rife.re` and `business.ool.fr`.\n5. **Phase Tracking**: Phases 1–4 marked complete, Phase 5 in progress with current Dovecot 2.4.1 LDAP syntax blocker details, and Phases 6–8 queued.\n6. **Open Risks & Action Items**: Queue backlog on `smtp-mtq-1`, LDAP relocation roadmap, contacts/address book location, and security recommendations."}
